From 8aee85b4e5a71b4b0a39977f5b490c70da8608ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:11:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 170/171] dynarmic: PS4 follow_plt_calls (BL through PLT stubs,
 on into short leaves behind them)

With follow_leaf_calls, a BL to a PLT stub (ADRP X16; LDR X17, [X16, #o]; ADD X16; BR X17) is
translated on into the stub; its BR then ends the block (guarded_indirect_links: a link to the
GOT slot's function). If the slot's function, as PeekCode reads it when translated (Translate's
new peek), is a short leaf and superblocks are on, the BR becomes a side exit taken when X17 isn't
that function (a block at the BR dispatches), the leaf is translated on, and its RET goes back
after the BL. A short leaf may read TPIDRRO_EL0/TPIDR_EL0 (MRS). Up to six branches followed and
eight pieces a block (two such calls), and a leaf call's pieces may repeat (two calls to one stub).
Bluey's "current thread" (MRS X8, TPIDRRO_EL0; LDR X0, [X8, #504]; RET) through a stub was 29%
of its samples; the harness's plt64: 186 host instructions an iteration (two calls) -> 100.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W5pLthrq7391gS4qodPV4u
